title: 'The Delphi method (RAND, 1950s): experts answer apart, in writing, in rounds, then see an anonymous summary of the others'' answers with reasons, and may revise.'
pid: a528072f-d2d9-4a1c-a905-fea760422a63
body: |2-
  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delphi_method
  Summary: Wikipedia, which flags the article as under-cited; RAND's
  page refused the fetch. Anonymity keeps "the authority, personality,
  or reputation of some participants from dominating others", and
  checks the bandwagon. "Overall the track record of the Delphi method
  is mixed", and a misinformed panel may "only add confidence to their
  ignorance". Took: proposals written apart, one round.
